## SQ-CBJ4-01 | CB mixins
@group A
@commands `grep -E "creativebrewing.mixins.json\|Mixin apply.*creativebrewing\|\[creativebrewing\]" logs/latest.log`; `grep -c "from creativebrewing.mixins.json" logs/debug.log`
@pass No mixin apply error; the 14 common mixins apply on a server (the 11 client ones do not load); none listed twice
@fails A compartment name not a mod id, or patcherMod still listing a moved mixin
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
bootreject creativebrewing\.mixins\.json.*(Error|error|failed)
shell grep -c "from creativebrewing.mixins.json" logs/debug.log; grep -o "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]* from creativebrewing.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | sed 's/Mixing //;s/ from.*//' | sort -u > cb_mx.txt; wc -l < cb_mx.txt; cat cb_mx.txt | tr '\n' ' '; echo; echo "also from CE:"; grep -o "Mixing [A-Za-z_.]* from creativeengineering.mixins.json" logs/debug.log | sed 's/Mixing //;s/ from.*//' | sort -u | comm -12 - cb_mx.txt; rm -f cb_mx.txt
look 14 common mixins (minus absent mods), none also from creativeengineering.mixins.json

## SQ-CBJ4-02 | config sections merged into the CB file
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep "\[swaps\] config sections" logs/latest.log`; read `config/creativebrewing-common.toml` and `config/creativeengineering-common.toml`; restart and grep `still has sections that moved`
@pass `merged from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativebrewing-common.toml` with the four sections; CB file has `quarkLine = false` and `reductionPerLevel = 0.3`; CE file no longer has them after the boot; second boot no WARN
@fails `mergeSections` ran after config load, or the section names differ
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
bootexpect \[swaps\] config sections .*alcohol.* merged from creativeengineering-common.toml into creativebrewing-common.toml
shell grep -E "\[swaps\] config sections" logs/latest.log | cut -c60-300; grep -nE "^\s*\[|quarkLine|reductionPerLevel|intervalSeconds|chancePerPiece" config/creativebrewing-common.toml; echo CE:; grep -nE "^\[(alcohol|effects|magic_resistance|copper_poisoning)\]" config/creativeengineering-common.toml || echo "CE has none of the four"
look CB file has [alcohol] quarkLine = false, [magic_resistance] reductionPerLevel = 0.3, copper 10 / 1.0; CE file lost the four

## SQ-CBJ4-03 | CE potions from CB, potion bucket dispenser
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/effect give @p minecraft:speed`, then `/give` a `creativeengineering:long_reach` potion (`/give @p minecraft:potion{Potion:"creativeengineering:long_reach"}`), `/give` a potion bucket and fire it from a dispenser
@pass Potion exists (CommonPotions registered from CB); dispenser places / splashes as before
@fails `CommonPotions` or `PotionBucketDispenser` not registered (CB `commonSetup`)
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
> give qa minecraft:potion{Potion:"creativeengineering:long_reach"}
> setblock {H1-4} {H2} {H3} minecraft:dispenser[facing=north]{Items:[{Slot:0b,id:"creativeengineering:potion_bucket",Count:1b,tag:{Potion:"minecraft:swiftness"}}]}
> setblock {H1-4} {H2} {H3+1} minecraft:redstone_block
sleep 1
> execute positioned {H1-4} {H2} {H3-1} if entity @e[type=minecraft:area_effect_cloud,distance=..6] run say CBJ4 bucket cloud
> execute positioned {H1-4} {H2} {H3-1} if entity @e[type=minecraft:item,distance=..3] run say CBJ4 bucket ejected
> data get block {H1-4} {H2} {H3} Items
expect Gave 1 +.*to qa
expect CBJ4 bucket cloud|minecraft:bucket
reject CBJ4 bucket ejected
reject Unknown (item|potion)|Invalid

## SQ-CBJ4-04 | effect remap from the CB file
@group A
@commands Same boot: `/effect give @p upgrade_aquatic:insomnia` and `/effect give @p neapolitan:agility` (if loaded), `/data get entity @p ActiveEffects`
@pass Insomnia refused, Agility swapped to `vinery:climbing_effect` ([effects] read from the CB file)
@fails `LivingEntityEffectRemapMixin` not applied, or EffectRules reading the wrong config
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
> effect give qa upgrade_aquatic:insomnia 30
> effect give qa neapolitan:agility 30
> data get entity qa ActiveEffects
look Insomnia refused, Agility swapped to vinery:climbing_effect (Id of that effect in the ActiveEffects reply)

## SQ-CBJ4-05 | copper poisoning
@group A
@commands Same boot: wear one fully oxidized Everything Copper piece with `[copper_poisoning] intervalSeconds = 10`, `chancePerPiece = 1.0` in the scratch CB file; wait 30 s
@pass Poison applied
@fails `CopperPoisoningHandler` not registered
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
> effect clear qa
> item replace entity qa armor.head with everythingcopper:copper_helmet{state:"oxidized"}
sleep 40
> data get entity qa ActiveEffects
expect Id: 19
look poison (Id 19) applied within 40 s at interval 10, chance 1.0

## SQ-CBJ4-06 | lingerification list, DragonBreathBrewing
@group A
@commands Same boot: `grep -E "DragonBreathBrewing\|Lingerification\|lingerification_list" logs/latest.log`; `/reload`
@pass No error; the lingerification list recipe loads from the CB jar (`creativeengineering:lingerification_list`)
@fails `data/creativeengineering/recipes/lingerification_list.json` missing from the CB jar
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
shell grep -E "DragonBreathBrewing|Lingerification|lingerification_list" logs/latest.log | grep -iE "error|fail|exception" | head -3; unzip -l mods/creativebrewing-1.0.0.jar | grep -c "data/creativeengineering/recipes/lingerification_list.json"
look no error lines; the CB jar holds the lingerification list (1)

## SQ-CBJ4-07 | Magic Resistance cuts magic damage by 30 % (iron golems: perfBot bots are invulnerable)
@group A
@commands Same boot: hit a player with Magic Resistance I with `/damage`-like magic (splash Harming)
@pass Damage cut by 30 % (scratch value)
@fails `MagicResistanceEffect` not on the FORGE bus
@from batches/r1101/cs4_boot3.qb
> difficulty normal
> summon minecraft:iron_golem {H1-12} {H2} {H3+4} {Tags:["mrC"],NoAI:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b}
> summon minecraft:iron_golem {H1-12} {H2} {H3+8} {Tags:["mrB"],NoAI:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b}
sleep 2
> effect give @e[tag=mrB,limit=1] creativeengineering:magic_resistance 60 0
> effect give @e[tag=mrC,limit=1] minecraft:instant_damage 1 0
> effect give @e[tag=mrB,limit=1] minecraft:instant_damage 1 0
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[tag=mrC,limit=1] Health
> data get entity @e[tag=mrB,limit=1] Health
> difficulty peaceful
expect 94\.0f
expect 95\.8f

